    <!-- Status info sheet -->
    <string name="info_level_what">How deep the flood water is on the street, measured by the sensor mounted above the road. 0 cm means the street is dry.</string>
    <string name="info_level_safe">Safe · up to %1$s</string>
    <string name="info_level_safe_text">Ankle to below-knee deep. You can usually walk or drive through slowly.</string>
    <string name="info_level_warning">Warning · %1$s to %2$s</string>
    <string name="info_level_warning_text">Knee deep. Hard to walk, small cars may stall. Avoid if you can.</string>
    <string name="info_level_critical">Critical · above %1$s</string>
    <string name="info_level_critical_text">Waist deep and up. Dangerous: don\'t walk or drive through.</string>
    <string name="info_level_tip">\"%% of threshold\" compares the water now to the Critical level (%1$s = 100%%).</string>

    <string name="info_risk_what">How dangerous this street is right now, based on the water level.</string>
    <string name="info_risk_safe_text">Water is below %1$s. Normal, but stay careful in the rain.</string>
    <string name="info_risk_warning_text">Water is between %1$s and %2$s. Be careful and avoid the street if you can.</string>
    <string name="info_risk_critical_text">Water is above %1$s. Stay away from the area.</string>
    <string name="info_risk_offline_text">The sensor isn\'t sending data right now, so the risk is unknown. Be careful.</string>
    <string name="info_risk_tip">You get a notification when a street turns Warning or Dangerous (if flood alerts are on in Settings).</string>

    <string name="info_rise_what">How fast the water is going up or down, worked out from the last 15 minutes of readings.</string>
    <string name="info_rise_rising">+ cm/hr · rising</string>
    <string name="info_rise_rising_text">Water is going up. \"+6 cm/hr\" means about 6 cm higher in an hour. If it keeps rising, the box shows when it could reach the next level, like \"Warning in ~25 min\".</string>
    <string name="info_rise_steady_text">Water is barely changing (less than %1$s per hour).</string>
    <string name="info_rise_falling">- cm/hr · falling</string>
    <string name="info_rise_measuring_text">The app needs a few minutes of readings first.</string>
    <string name="info_rise_tip">A fast rise during heavy rain is an early sign of flooding, even if the level is still Safe.</string>

    <string name="info_rain_what">What the rain sensor on this street is feeling right now. Wetter sensor = heavier rain.</string>
    <string name="info_rain_none_text">The sensor is dry.</string>
    <string name="info_rain_light_text">Drizzle or light showers. Little effect on flooding.</string>
    <string name="info_rain_moderate_text">Steady rain. Water may start to collect on low streets.</string>
    <string name="info_rain_heavy_text">Downpour. Water can rise quickly: watch the Rise Rate and Risk Level.</string>
    <string name="info_rain_tip">Rain alone doesn\'t mean flooding. Check the Water Level to see how deep it really is.</string>

