    <string name="about_how_sensors_title">Sensors measure the street</string>
    <string name="about_how_sensors_text">Each street has an ultrasonic sensor mounted 94 cm above the road and a rain sensor. Water level = 94 cm minus the distance to the water. Readings go to the cloud every few seconds.</string>
    <string name="about_how_levels_title">Three risk levels</string>
    <string name="about_how_levels_text">Safe: up to %1$d cm (ankle to below the knee). Warning: %1$d–%2$d cm (knee deep). Critical: above %2$d cm (waist deep and up).</string>
    <string name="about_how_rise_title">Rise rate</string>
    <string name="about_how_forecast_title">Flood Forecast (Linear Regression)</string>
    <string name="about_how_forecast_text">Predicts the water level 30 minutes ahead from the level now and how much it changed over the last 5, 15 and 30 minutes.</string>
    <string name="about_how_risk_title">Flood Risk (Lasso Regression)</string>
    <string name="about_how_risk_text">Combines the water level with rain (recent readings, rate of change and cumulative rainfall) to rate each street Low, Warning or Critical for the next 30 minutes.</string>
    <string name="about_how_rain_title">Rain Forecast</string>
    <string name="about_how_rain_text">Uses the street\'s own rain sensor to show the last 30 minutes of rain and what to expect 30 minutes from now.</string>
    <string name="about_how_alerts_title">Flood alerts</string>
    <string name="about_how_alerts_text">A background monitor watches all four streets and notifies you when one rises to Warning or Critical, even when the app is closed.</string>
    <string name="about_how_chart_title">Flood chart and 7-day forecast</string>
    <string name="about_how_chart_text">The chart shows each street\'s water level over time (recorded sample data and live readings); Home shows the week\'s chance of rain.</string>
    <string name="about_src_sensors">ESP32 with ultrasonic water-level and rain sensors on Sealion, Samaritan, Swingfire and Striker Streets</string>
    <string name="about_src_rtdb">Live sensor readings, recorded sample data and user accounts</string>
    <string name="about_src_fcm">Delivers flood alert notifications</string>
    <string name="about_src_analytics">Anonymous usage statistics, only if you agree</string>
    <string name="about_src_models">Forecast models trained on the recorded flood data (simulated sample data, Oct 13–28, 2026)</string>
